{
  "rationale": "The plant separates sensing (uncontrollable obstacle events) from motion (controllable pulses). The specification binds each perception outcome to a single safe, progress-oriented action, enforcing conservative recovery and rapid return to exploration. Only one controllable is enabled per state, and all obstacle events force a recovery state before resuming exploration.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model perception and motion as a single plant automaton with all event outcomes and motion commands.",
    "Specification automaton enforces: (1) forward/random_walk in clear, (2) move_backward on front obstacle, (3) rotate_clockwise on left obstacle, (4) rotate_counterclockwise on right obstacle, (5) full_rotate only after repeated blockages, (6) rapid return to exploration after recovery."
  ],
